<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian govt to review pension deeming rates.</title>
<headline>Australian govt to review pension deeming rates.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Treasurer Peter Costello said on Wednesday the government would review deeming rates on pensions following the latest central bank easing of interest rates.</p>
<p>&quot;What this means is that we will now be reviewing deeming rates in the lead up to the next pension adjustment to make sure the deeming rates are set on a realistic basis, taking into account these low interest rates,&quot; Costello told reporters.  </p>
<p>The official pensioner deeming rate is an earnings rate, decided by the federal government, which is deemed to apply to pensioners' bank accounts and is used to means test age pensions.</p>
<p>Pensioner security accounts held by banks pay interest at the government's pensioner deeming rate of seven percent on amounts over A$30,000.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
